{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HRYYUGKue8fDMr2FJaMjWQ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Cinescope — cinema seat booking\n\nA web application for booking cinema seats. A customer picks a day and a movie screening,\nchooses seats on a map of the auditorium, reviews the tickets, fills in their details and\npays.\n\nThis file is the complete specification. The work is split into tickets in\n[`tickets/`](tickets/README.md); each ticket points back to the sections below and lists\nthe acceptance criteria it has to satisfy.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project setup\n\nThe framework, the libraries and the state of the scaffold are described in\n[`stack.md`](stack.md). The application is the Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`.\n\nAll commands run from the workspace root:\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `pnpm install` | installs dependencies (already done) |\n| `pnpm nx serve cinescope` | starts the application at `http://localhost:4200` |\n| `pnpm api` | starts the backend at `http://localhost:3000` |\n| `pnpm nx build cinescope` | production build — must succeed |\n| `pnpm nx test cinescope` | unit tests (Vitest) |\n| `pnpm nx lint cinescope` | ESLint |\n\nRules for the environment:\n\n- The package manager is pnpm. Do not use `npm` or `yarn`.\n- The application is served at `http://localhost:4200`. Do not change the port.\n- Do not add dependencies. Everything the application needs is already installed.\n- Do not edit `db.json` by hand. It is the backend's data.\n- The application is desktop-only (viewport 1280 × 720 or larger). All user-facing text is\n  in English.\n\n### 1.1 UI library\n\nUse components of the UI library named in [`stack.md`](stack.md) for every button (including the day buttons and the\nscreening buttons), text field, checkbox, toast and for the datepicker. The seat map, the\nlegend and the selected-seats panel are drawn by the application itself.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Backend\n\nThe backend is [`json-server`](https://github.com/typicode/json-server/tree/v0) 0.17.4\nserving `db.json` from the workspace root. Start it with `pnpm api` and keep it running\nwhile you work on the application.\n\n- **Base URL:** `http://localhost:3000`\n- CORS is enabled; the application calls the base URL directly.\n- Every response is JSON. Requests with a body send `Content-Type: application/json`.\n- `json-server` writes every successful `POST` into `db.json`. That is expected.\n\n### 2.1 Data model\n\n```ts\ninterface Movie {\n  id: number;\n  title: string;            // \"The Silent Harbor\"\n  genre: string;            // \"Drama\"\n  runtimeMinutes: number;   // 128\n  format: 'PL dubbing' | 'PL subtitles';\n}\n\ninterface Screening {\n  id: number;\n  movieId: number;          // references Movie.id\n  date: string;             // \"2026-09-15\" (YYYY-MM-DD)\n  time: string;             // \"16:00\" (HH:mm, 24-hour)\n  occupiedSeats: string[];  // seat identifiers already sold, e.g. [\"R3C7\", \"R15C5\", \"R15C6\"]\n}\n\ninterface Reservation {\n  id: number;               // assigned by the backend\n  screeningId: number;\n  seats: string[];          // seat identifiers, a couch contributes both of its identifiers\n  customer: {\n    firstName: string;\n    lastName: string;\n    email: string;\n    phone: string;          // \"\" when not provided\n  };\n  totalPrice: number;       // in PLN, e.g. 121\n}\n```\n\n**Seat identifier** — `R<row>C<column>`, for example `R7C12` is row 7, column 12. A couch\noccupies two identifiers: the couch over columns 5–6 of row 15 is `R15C5` + `R15C6`.\n\n### 2.2 Endpoints\n\n| Method | Path | Returns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GET` | `/movies` | `Movie[]` — 5 movies |\n| `GET` | `/movies/:id` | `Movie`, or `404` |\n| `GET` | `/screenings` | `Screening[]` — all screenings, in no guaranteed order |\n| `GET` | `/screenings?date=:date` | `Screening[]` of one day, e.g. `?date=2026-09-15` |\n| `GET` | `/screenings?movieId=:movieId` | `Screening[]` of one movie |\n| `GET` | `/screenings/:id` | `Screening`, or `404` |\n| `POST` | `/reservations` | `201` with the created `Reservation` |\n\n`GET /screenings/1` returns:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"movieId\": 1,\n  \"date\": \"2026-09-15\",\n  \"time\": \"16:00\",\n  \"occupiedSeats\": [\"R3C7\", \"R3C8\", \"R3C9\", \"R6C12\", \"R6C13\", \"R11C21\", \"R11C22\", \"R15C5\", \"R15C6\"]\n}\n```\n\n`POST /reservations` request body:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"screeningId\": 1,\n  \"seats\": [\"R7C12\", \"R15C1\", \"R15C2\"],\n  \"customer\": {\n    \"firstName\": \"Anna\",\n    \"lastName\": \"Kowalska\",\n    \"email\": \"anna.kowalska@example.com\",\n    \"phone\": \"123456789\"\n  },\n  \"totalPrice\": 121\n}\n```\n\nThe response is the same object with an `id` added. Any network error or any status other\nthan `2xx` is a failed request. Creating a reservation does not change the screening's\n`occupiedSeats`; the application makes no other write requests.\n\n**Dates.** The screenings in `db.json` are between 15 and 21 September 2026. The\napplication always works from the browser's current date, so on other dates the movie list\nmay show `No screenings on this day` for every day it offers — that is expected. Do not\nchange `db.json`, and do not change the date logic to see screenings.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Screens and navigation\n\n| # | Route | Screen |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `/` | Movie list |\n| 2 | `/screenings/:id/seats` | Seat selection for screening `:id` |\n| 3 | `/screenings/:id/summary` | Ticket summary |\n| 4 | `/screenings/:id/checkout` | Customer details and payment |\n| 5 | `/confirmation` | Payment successful |\n\nAny other URL redirects to `/`.\n\n### 3.1 The booking\n\nThe booking is kept in `sessionStorage`, so it survives a page reload. It holds the\nscreening id, the selected seats, the values typed into the checkout form and, once paid,\nthe customer's email address. A booking is *in progress* until it is paid.\n\n| Entering… | allowed when | otherwise |\n|---|---|---|\n| route 2 | the screening exists | redirect to `/` |\n| routes 3 and 4 | the booking is unpaid, belongs to this screening id and has at least one seat | redirect to `/` |\n| route 5 | the booking is paid | redirect to `/` |\n\nThese checks run when a route is entered, including by a reload — not while the customer\nstays on a screen. Paying therefore opens `/confirmation` without the checkout screen\nredirecting first.\n\n- Opening the seat map of a screening shows the selection of the booking in progress when\n  it belongs to that screening. Otherwise — no booking, a booking for another screening, or\n  a paid booking — it starts a new, empty booking for that screening, discarding the\n  previous one (with its form values) once the screening has loaded.\n- `Cancel` on the seat map and `Continue` on the confirmation screen clear the booking.\n\n### 3.2 Toasts\n\nShort messages are shown as toasts. Only one toast is visible at a time — a new toast\nreplaces the current one. A toast stays visible for 4 seconds and then disappears.\n\n### 3.3 Date formats\n\n| Name | Format | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| ISO date | `YYYY-MM-DD` | `2026-09-15` |\n| time | `HH:mm`, 24-hour, as in the data | `16:00` |\n| show date | `<Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>` — English weekday in full, day without a leading zero, English month in three letters | `Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00` |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Movie list (`/`)\n\nPage layout, top to bottom: the day picker, then the movie list.\n\n### 4.1 Day picker\n\n- Five day buttons: `Today`, then the next four days labelled with their English weekday in\n  full. If today is Tuesday: `Today`, `Wednesday`, `Thursday`, `Friday`, `Saturday`.\n- After them, a datepicker for choosing any other date. Dates before today cannot be\n  chosen; there is no upper limit.\n- Exactly one day is selected at a time. When the selected day is one of the five, its\n  button is shown as selected; when it was chosen in the datepicker and is not one of the\n  five, no button is selected and the datepicker shows the date.\n- The selected day is part of the URL: `/?date=<ISO date>`. Choosing a day updates the URL.\n  `/` without `date`, with a date that is not a valid ISO date, or with a date before today\n  selects today.\n\n### 4.2 Movies\n\nMovies and screenings are loaded from the backend each time the screen opens.\n\n- **Loading** — while the requests are in flight the screen shows the text `Loading…` and\n  no movie cards.\n- **Error** — if a request fails, the screen shows the text `Failed to load movies` and a\n  `Retry` button. `Retry` issues the requests again (showing the loading indicator).\n- **Loaded** — a vertical list of movie cards: one per movie that has at least one\n  screening on the selected day, in the order the backend returns the movies. Each card\n  shows:\n  - the title,\n  - the genre,\n  - the runtime as `<runtimeMinutes> min`, e.g. `128 min`,\n  - the format, exactly as in the data: `PL dubbing` or `PL subtitles`,\n  - one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with its time,\n    e.g. `16:00`, ordered by time.\n- **Empty** — when no movie has a screening on the selected day, the screen shows the text\n  `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n\nClicking a screening button opens `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Seat selection (`/screenings/:id/seats`)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XNLEEMidpH8S14k4DJag8E","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"53dd3ba3-7198-4462-93ca-789006499670","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:48:19.812Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 01"}
