{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012sCi5HkBmSz8niXCPqGYsQ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Stack\n\nThe workspace is an Nx 23 monorepo. The application is the Nx project `cinescope` in\n`apps/cinescope`, generated with the Nx Angular application generator: **Angular 22**,\nstandalone components, zoneless, Angular Router with an empty route list, SCSS, Vitest for\nunit tests and ESLint. **Angular Material 22** and the Angular CDK are installed, a Material\ntheme is applied in `styles.scss`, and the native date adapter is provided for the\ndatepicker. It is ready to run; build the application on top of it.\n----\n# Tickets\n\nWork through the tickets in order. A ticket can start once every ticket in its\n**Blocked by** line is done. The specification is [`../README.md`](../README.md); each\nticket names the sections it implements and the acceptance criteria it must satisfy.\n\n| # | Ticket | Blocked by | Criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | [Movie list and day picker](01-movie-list.md) | — | 11 |\n| 02 | [Auditorium map](02-auditorium-map.md) | 01 | 13 |\n| 03 | [Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel](03-seat-selection.md) | 02 | 14 |\n| 04 | [Booking and summary](04-booking-summary.md) | 03 | 16 |\n| 05 | [Checkout and payment](05-checkout.md) | 04 | 13 |\n| 06 | [Confirmation and booking lifecycle](06-confirmation.md) | 05 | 2 |\n| 07 | [Final pass](07-final-pass.md) | 01–06 | all |\n\nA ticket is done when every box in it is ticked and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\n----\n# 03: Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel\n\n**What to build:** On the seat map the customer selects and deselects seats and couches, up to 10 seats per booking with a couch counting as 2. Unavailable seats cannot be selected. Exceeding the limit shows a toast. Every state has its colour, the legend explains them, and the selected-seats panel lists the current selection by row.\n\n**Specification:** sections 3.2, 5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 9.2, 9.6, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 02 — Auditorium map.\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-16 — Seats listed in `occupiedSeats` for the screening are rendered unavailable and cannot be selected.\n- [ ] AC-17 — A couch is unavailable when either of its two seat identifiers is in `occupiedSeats`.\n- [ ] AC-18 — Clicking an available seat selects it; clicking it again deselects it.\n- [ ] AC-19 — Clicking a couch selects both of its seats as one unit; it cannot be half-selected.\n- [ ] AC-20 — Selection is capped at 10 seats; a couch counts as 2.\n- [ ] AC-21 — A click that would exceed 10 seats is ignored and shows the toast `Maximum 10 seats per booking`.\n- [ ] AC-22 — At the cap, already selected seats and couches can still be deselected.\n- [ ] AC-23 — The legend lists exactly `Available`, `Selected`, `Unavailable`, `Accessible`.\n- [ ] AC-24 — Available seats use `#2E7D32`.\n- [ ] AC-25 — Selected seats use `#F9A825`.\n- [ ] AC-26 — Unavailable seats use `#C62828`.\n- [ ] AC-27 — Accessible seats use `#1565C0`.\n- [ ] AC-58 — Between the seat map and the `Cancel` / `Continue` buttons, the selected-seats panel shows `Selected seats: <n>` and one `Row <r>: <seats>` line per row, updated on every selection change.\n- [ ] AC-66 — Every seat-selection identifier in section 9.2, and the toast identifier in section 9.6, is present with the exact names and values given there.\n----\napps/cinescope/src:\napp\nindex.html\nmain.ts\nstyles.scss\n\napps/cinescope/src/app:\napi.ts\napp.config.ts\napp.html\napp.routes.ts\napp.scss\napp.spec.ts\napp.ts\ndates.spec.ts\ndates.ts\nmodels.ts\nmovie-list\nseat-selection\n\napps/cinescope/src/app/movie-list:\nmovie-list.html\nmovie-list.scss\nmovie-list.ts\n\napps/cinescope/src/app/seat-selection:\nauditorium.spec.ts\nauditorium.ts\nseat-selection.html\nseat-selection.scss\nseat-selection.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JK4dFtrc8FqNwCijco2niZ","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"9a8736b2-6937-44a8-823e-8dcaf8b07e1f","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:53:48.896Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 03"}
