{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hz1cfHNZK1PWvzkrdRAcsq","type":"tool_result","content":"290\t\n291\t### 5.2 Selecting seats\n292\t\n293\t- Clicking an available seat or couch selects it; clicking a selected one deselects it.\n294\t- Clicking an unavailable seat or couch does nothing.\n295\t- A booking holds at most 10 seats. A couch counts as 2 seats.\n296\t- A click that would take the booking above 10 seats is ignored and shows the toast\n297\t  `Maximum 10 seats per booking`. Selected seats and couches can always be deselected.\n298\t\n299\t### 5.3 Colours and legend\n300\t\n301\tEach seat and couch is painted, as its background colour, with the colour of its state:\n302\t\n303\t| State | Colour | Applies to |\n304\t|---|---|---|\n305\t| Available | `#2E7D32` | free regular seats and free couches |\n306\t| Selected | `#F9A825` | any selected seat or couch |\n307\t| Unavailable | `#C62828` | any seat or couch in `occupiedSeats` |\n308\t| Accessible | `#1565C0` | free, unselected accessible seats |\n309\t\n310\tHovering or focusing a seat must not change its background colour.\n311\t\n312\tUnder the auditorium, a legend lists these four states — `Available`, `Selected`,\n313\t`Unavailable`, `Accessible` — each with a swatch of its colour.\n314\t\n315\t### 5.4 Prices\n316\t\n317\t| Seat | Price |\n318\t|---|---|\n319\t| rows 1–5, including the accessible seats | `25.00 PLN` |\n320\t| rows 6–10 | `32.00 PLN` |\n321\t| rows 11–14 | `39.00 PLN` |\n322\t| one couch in row 15 (two seats) | `89.00 PLN` |\n323\t\n324\tPrices are always printed with two decimals and the `PLN` suffix: `25.00 PLN`.\n325\t\n326\t### 5.5 Selected-seats panel\n327\t\n328\tShows the current selection and updates on every click:\n329\t\n330\t```\n331\tSelected seats: 4\n332\tRow 7: 11, 12\n333\tRow 15: 1-2\n334\t```\n335\t\n336\t- The first line is `Selected seats: <n>`, where `<n>` counts seats (a couch counts as 2).\n337\t- Then one line per row that has a selection, rows in ascending order:\n338\t  `Row <r>: <seats>`, the seats in ascending column order, separated by `, `; a seat is its\n339\t  column number, a couch is `<a>-<b>`.\n340\t- With nothing selected the panel shows `Selected seats: 0` and no row lines.\n341\t\n342\t### 5.6 Actions\n343\t\n344\t- `Cancel` clears the booking and opens `/`.\n345\t- `Continue` opens `/screenings/:id/summary`. With no seat selected it does nothing (it may\n346\t  be disabled).\n347\t\n348\t---\n349\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JK4dFtrc8FqNwCijco2niZ","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"7a9c9987-d223-4c33-aa46-26ab046af80b","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:53:50.249Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 03"}
