{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNPUyYQ8MqYEKfprPsf4Ju","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Cinescope — cinema seat booking\n2\t\n3\tA web application for booking cinema seats. A customer picks a day and a movie screening,\n4\tchooses seats on a map of the auditorium, reviews the tickets, fills in their details and\n5\tpays.\n6\t\n7\tThis file is the complete specification. The work is split into tickets in\n8\t[`tickets/`](tickets/README.md); each ticket points back to the sections below and lists\n9\tthe acceptance criteria it has to satisfy.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## 1. Project setup\n14\t\n15\tThe framework, the libraries and the state of the scaffold are described in\n16\t[`stack.md`](stack.md). The application is the Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`.\n17\t\n18\tAll commands run from the workspace root:\n19\t\n20\t| Command | What it does |\n21\t|---|---|\n22\t| `pnpm install` | installs dependencies (already done) |\n23\t| `pnpm nx serve cinescope` | starts the application at `http://localhost:4200` |\n24\t| `pnpm api` | starts the backend at `http://localhost:3000` |\n25\t| `pnpm nx build cinescope` | production build — must succeed |\n26\t| `pnpm nx test cinescope` | unit tests (Vitest) |\n27\t| `pnpm nx lint cinescope` | ESLint |\n28\t\n29\tRules for the environment:\n30\t\n31\t- The package manager is pnpm. Do not use `npm` or `yarn`.\n32\t- The application is served at `http://localhost:4200`. Do not change the port.\n33\t- Do not add dependencies. Everything the application needs is already installed.\n34\t- Do not edit `db.json` by hand. It is the backend's data.\n35\t- The application is desktop-only (viewport 1280 × 720 or larger). All user-facing text is\n36\t  in English.\n37\t\n38\t### 1.1 UI library\n39\t\n40\tUse components of the UI library named in [`stack.md`](stack.md) for every button (including the day buttons and the\n41\tscreening buttons), text field, checkbox, toast and for the datepicker. The seat map, the\n42\tlegend and the selected-seats panel are drawn by the application itself.\n43\t\n44\t---\n45\t\n46\t## 2. Backend\n47\t\n48\tThe backend is [`json-server`](https://github.com/typicode/json-server/tree/v0) 0.17.4\n49\tserving `db.json` from the workspace root. Start it with `pnpm api` and keep it running\n50\twhile you work on the application.\n51\t\n52\t- **Base URL:** `http://localhost:3000`\n53\t- CORS is enabled; the application calls the base URL directly.\n54\t- Every response is JSON. Requests with a body send `Content-Type: application/json`.\n55\t- `json-server` writes every successful `POST` into `db.json`. That is expected.\n56\t\n57\t### 2.1 Data model\n58\t\n59\t```ts\n60\tinterface Movie {\n61\t  id: number;\n62\t  title: string;            // \"The Silent Harbor\"\n63\t  genre: string;            // \"Drama\"\n64\t  runtimeMinutes: number;   // 128\n65\t  format: 'PL dubbing' | 'PL subtitles';\n66\t}\n67\t\n68\tinterface Screening {\n69\t  id: number;\n70\t  movieId: number;          // references Movie.id\n71\t  date: string;             // \"2026-09-15\" (YYYY-MM-DD)\n72\t  time: string;             // \"16:00\" (HH:mm, 24-hour)\n73\t  occupiedSeats: string[];  // seat identifiers already sold, e.g. [\"R3C7\", \"R15C5\", \"R15C6\"]\n74\t}\n75\t\n76\tinterface Reservation {\n77\t  id: number;               // assigned by the backend\n78\t  screeningId: number;\n79\t  seats: string[];          // seat identifiers, a couch contributes both of its identifiers\n80\t  customer: {\n81\t    firstName: string;\n82\t    lastName: string;\n83\t    email: string;\n84\t    phone: string;          // \"\" when not provided\n85\t  };\n86\t  totalPrice: number;       // in PLN, e.g. 121\n87\t}\n88\t```\n89\t\n90\t**Seat identifier** — `R<row>C<column>`, for example `R7C12` is row 7, column 12. A couch\n91\toccupies two identifiers: the couch over columns 5–6 of row 15 is `R15C5` + `R15C6`.\n92\t\n93\t### 2.2 Endpoints\n94\t\n95\t| Method | Path | Returns |\n96\t|---|---|---|\n97\t| `GET` | `/movies` | `Movie[]` — 5 movies |\n98\t| `GET` | `/movies/:id` | `Movie`, or `404` |\n99\t| `GET` | `/screenings` | `Screening[]` — all screenings, in no guaranteed order |\n100\t| `GET` | `/screenings?date=:date` | `Screening[]` of one day, e.g. `?date=2026-09-15` |\n101\t| `GET` | `/screenings?movieId=:movieId` | `Screening[]` of one movie |\n102\t| `GET` | `/screenings/:id` | `Screening`, or `404` |\n103\t| `POST` | `/reservations` | `201` with the created `Reservation` |\n104\t\n105\t`GET /screenings/1` returns:\n106\t\n107\t```json\n108\t{\n109\t  \"id\": 1,\n110\t  \"movieId\": 1,\n111\t  \"date\": \"2026-09-15\",\n112\t  \"time\": \"16:00\",\n113\t  \"occupiedSeats\": [\"R3C7\", \"R3C8\", \"R3C9\", \"R6C12\", \"R6C13\", \"R11C21\", \"R11C22\", \"R15C5\", \"R15C6\"]\n114\t}\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\t`POST /reservations` request body:\n118\t\n119\t```json\n120\t{\n121\t  \"screeningId\": 1,\n122\t  \"seats\": [\"R7C12\", \"R15C1\", \"R15C2\"],\n123\t  \"customer\": {\n124\t    \"firstName\": \"Anna\",\n125\t    \"lastName\": \"Kowalska\",\n126\t    \"email\": \"anna.kowalska@example.com\",\n127\t    \"phone\": \"123456789\"\n128\t  },\n129\t  \"totalPrice\": 121\n130\t}\n131\t```\n132\t\n133\tThe response is the same object with an `id` added. Any network error or any status other\n134\tthan `2xx` is a failed request. Creating a reservation does not change the screening's\n135\t`occupiedSeats`; the application makes no other write requests.\n136\t\n137\t**Dates.** The screenings in `db.json` are between 15 and 21 September 2026. The\n138\tapplication always works from the browser's current date, so on other dates the movie list\n139\tmay show `No screenings on this day` for every day it offers — that is expected. Do not\n140\tchange `db.json`, and do not change the date logic to see screenings.\n141\t\n142\t---\n143\t\n144\t## 3. Screens and navigation\n145\t\n146\t| # | Route | Screen |\n147\t|---|---|---|\n148\t| 1 | `/` | Movie list |\n149\t| 2 | `/screenings/:id/seats` | Seat selection for screening `:id` |\n150\t| 3 | `/screenings/:id/summary` | Ticket summary |\n151\t| 4 | `/screenings/:id/checkout` | Customer details and payment |\n152\t| 5 | `/confirmation` | Payment successful |\n153\t\n154\tAny other URL redirects to `/`.\n155\t\n156\t### 3.1 The booking\n157\t\n158\tThe booking is kept in `sessionStorage`, so it survives a page reload. It holds the\n159\tscreening id, the selected seats, the values typed into the checkout form and, once paid,\n160\tthe customer's email address. A booking is *in progress* until it is paid.\n161\t\n162\t| Entering… | allowed when | otherwise |\n163\t|---|---|---|\n164\t| route 2 | the screening exists | redirect to `/` |\n165\t| routes 3 and 4 | the booking is unpaid, belongs to this screening id and has at least one seat | redirect to `/` |\n166\t| route 5 | the booking is paid | redirect to `/` |\n167\t\n168\tThese checks run when a route is entered, including by a reload — not while the customer\n169\tstays on a screen. Paying therefore opens `/confirmation` without the checkout screen\n170\tredirecting first.\n171\t\n172\t- Opening the seat map of a screening shows the selection of the booking in progress when\n173\t  it belongs to that screening. Otherwise — no booking, a booking for another screening, or\n174\t  a paid booking — it starts a new, empty booking for that screening, discarding the\n175\t  previous one (with its form values) once the screening has loaded.\n176\t- `Cancel` on the seat map and `Continue` on the confirmation screen clear the booking.\n177\t\n178\t### 3.2 Toasts\n179\t\n180\tShort messages are shown as toasts. Only one toast is visible at a time — a new toast\n181\treplaces the current one. A toast stays visible for 4 seconds and then disappears.\n182\t\n183\t### 3.3 Date formats\n184\t\n185\t| Name | Format | Example |\n186\t|---|---|---|\n187\t| ISO date | `YYYY-MM-DD` | `2026-09-15` |\n188\t| time | `HH:mm`, 24-hour, as in the data | `16:00` |\n189\t| show date | `<Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>` — English weekday in full, day without a leading zero, English month in three letters | `Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00` |\n190\t\n191\t---\n192\t\n193\t## 4. Movie list (`/`)\n194\t\n195\tPage layout, top to bottom: the day picker, then the movie list.\n196\t\n197\t### 4.1 Day picker\n198\t\n199\t- Five day buttons: `Today`, then the next four days labelled with their English weekday in\n200\t  full. If today is Tuesday: `Today`, `Wednesday`, `Thursday`, `Friday`, `Saturday`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TuLQ4ngmNdgyyFYRo1pSPq","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"364f1112-1207-4b43-8f5b-7016feeb8f0e","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:56:19.582Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 04"}
