{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTYHd96dGUjg6gNuxE9f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bmxk7AqMM8tTjXEpae8KcQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-selection/seat-selection.html apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-selection/seat-selection.scss && echo ---- && cat apps/cinescope/src/app/app.ts apps/cinescope/src/app/app.html apps/cinescope/src/app/app.spec.ts && echo ---- && sed -n 200,233p spec/README.md && echo ---- && cat spec/tickets/03-seat-selection.md","description":"Read seat selection, app shell, and ticket 03"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13538,"cache_read_input_tokens":28177,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13538,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TuLQ4ngmNdgyyFYRo1pSPq","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"e67e1948-f071-450b-bb1c-9d86f5f15ea6","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:56:22.014Z","request_id":"req_011ChTYHcxgt89BMo2o12Tuc","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 04"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bmxk7AqMM8tTjXEpae8KcQ","type":"tool_result","content":"@if (screening()) {\n  <section class=\"seat-selection-page\">\n    <h1 class=\"title\" data-testid=\"seat-map-title\">Choose your seats</h1>\n    <p class=\"subtitle\" data-testid=\"seat-map-subtitle\">Show Date: {{ showDate() }}</p>\n\n    <div class=\"auditorium\">\n      <p class=\"seat-limit\" data-testid=\"seat-limit-info\">You can reserve up to 10 seats per reservation</p>\n      <div class=\"screen\" data-testid=\"screen-indicator\">SCREEN</div>\n\n      <div class=\"seat-map\" data-testid=\"seat-map\">\n        @for (row of rows(); track row.row) {\n          <div class=\"seat-row\" data-testid=\"seat-row\" [attr.data-row]=\"row.row\">\n            <span class=\"row-label row-label-left\" data-testid=\"row-label-left\" [attr.data-row]=\"row.row\">{{ row.row }}</span>\n            @for (cell of row.cells; track $index) {\n              @switch (cell.kind) {\n                @case ('seat') {\n                  <button\n                    type=\"button\"\n                    class=\"seat\"\n                    data-testid=\"seat\"\n                    [style.grid-column]=\"cell.gridColumn\"\n                    [attr.data-row]=\"cell.row\"\n                    [attr.data-column]=\"cell.column\"\n                    [attr.data-state]=\"cell.state\"\n                    [disabled]=\"cell.state === 'unavailable'\"\n                    (click)=\"toggle(cell)\"\n                  >{{ cell.column }}</button>\n                }\n                @case ('couch') {\n                  <button\n                    type=\"button\"\n                    class=\"couch\"\n                    data-testid=\"couch\"\n                    [style.grid-column]=\"cell.gridColumn\"\n                    [attr.data-row]=\"cell.row\"\n                    [attr.data-column-start]=\"cell.columnStart\"\n                    [attr.data-column-end]=\"cell.columnEnd\"\n                    [attr.data-state]=\"cell.state\"\n                    [disabled]=\"cell.state === 'unavailable'\"\n                    (click)=\"toggle(cell)\"\n                  >{{ cell.columnStart }}-{{ cell.columnEnd }}</button>\n                }\n                @case ('aisle') {\n                  <div\n                    class=\"aisle\"\n                    data-testid=\"aisle\"\n                    [style.grid-column]=\"cell.gridColumn\"\n                    [attr.data-row]=\"cell.row\"\n                  ></div>\n                }\n              }\n            }\n            <span class=\"row-label row-label-right\" data-testid=\"row-label-right\" [attr.data-row]=\"row.row\">{{ row.row }}</span>\n          </div>\n        }\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <ul class=\"legend\" data-testid=\"legend\">\n      @for (item of legend; track item.state) {\n        <li class=\"legend-item\" data-testid=\"legend-item\" [attr.data-state]=\"item.state\">\n          <span class=\"legend-swatch\"></span>\n          <span>{{ item.label }}</span>\n        </li>\n      }\n    </ul>\n\n    <div class=\"selected-seats\" data-testid=\"selected-seats\">\n      <p class=\"selected-seats-count\" data-testid=\"selected-seats-count\">Selected seats: {{ selectedCount() }}</p>\n      @for (line of selectedRows(); track line.row) {\n        <p class=\"selected-seats-row\" data-testid=\"selected-seats-row\" [attr.data-row]=\"line.row\">Row {{ line.row }}: {{ line.seats.join(', ') }}</p>\n      }\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"actions\">\n      <button mat-stroked-button type=\"button\" data-testid=\"cancel-button\" (click)=\"cancel()\">Cancel</button>\n      <button\n        mat-flat-button\n        type=\"button\"\n        data-testid=\"continue-button\"\n        [disabled]=\"selectedCount() === 0\"\n        (click)=\"continueToSummary()\"\n      >Continue</button>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n}\n:host {\n  display: block;\n}\n\n.seat-selection-page {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 16px;\n  padding: 24px;\n}\n\n.title {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 28px;\n  font-weight: 500;\n}\n\n.subtitle {\n  margin: 0;\n  color: var(--mat-sys-on-surface-variant);\n}\n\n// Sized by the seat map, so the screen bar and the limit text centre over it.\n.auditorium {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 16px;\n  width: max-content;\n}\n\n.seat-limit {\n  margin: 0;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.screen {\n  align-self: stretch;\n  padding: 6px 0;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  background: var(--mat-sys-surface-variant);\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 14px;\n  letter-spacing: 4px;\n}\n\n.seat-map {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 6px;\n}\n\n// Tracks: label | cols 1-4 | aisle | cols 5-20 | aisle | cols 21-24 | label. See auditorium.ts.\n.seat-row {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 24px repeat(4, 32px) 68px repeat(16, 32px) 68px repeat(4, 32px) 24px;\n  grid-template-rows: 32px;\n  column-gap: 4px;\n  align-items: center;\n\n  > * {\n    grid-row: 1;\n  }\n}\n\n.row-label {\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: var(--mat-sys-on-surface-variant);\n}\n\n.row-label-left {\n  grid-column: 1;\n}\n\n.row-label-right {\n  grid-column: 28;\n}\n\n.seat,\n.couch {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 32px;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  border: 0;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  font: inherit;\n  font-size: 11px;\n  color: #fff;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n// A couch is one element spanning two columns, with rounder corners.\n.couch {\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  font-weight: 500;\n}\n\n// Each state sets one colour, used by seats, couches and legend swatches alike. Hover and focus\n// do not change it, and legend items (which also carry the state) are not painted.\n[data-state='available'] {\n  --state-colour: #2e7d32;\n}\n\n[data-state='accessible'] {\n  --state-colour: #1565c0;\n}\n\n[data-state='selected'] {\n  --state-colour: #f9a825;\n}\n\n[data-state='unavailable'] {\n  --state-colour: #c62828;\n}\n\n.seat,\n.couch,\n.legend-swatch {\n  background-color: var(--state-colour);\n}\n\n.seat[data-state='unavailable'],\n.couch[data-state='unavailable'] {\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n\n.seat[data-state='selected'],\n.couch[data-state='selected'] {\n  color: #212121;\n}\n\n.legend {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: 16px;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  list-style: none;\n}\n\n.legend-item {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 8px;\n  font-size: 14px;\n}\n\n.legend-swatch {\n  width: 16px;\n  height: 16px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n.selected-seats {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n\n.selected-seats-count,\n.selected-seats-row {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.actions {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 16px;\n}\n----\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core';\nimport { RouterOutlet } from '@angular/router';\n\n@Component({\n  imports: [RouterOutlet],\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  templateUrl: './app.html',\n  styleUrl: './app.scss',\n})\nexport class App {}\n<router-outlet />\nimport { TestBed } from '@angular/core/testing';\nimport { App } from './app';\n\ndescribe('App', () => {\n  beforeEach(async () => {\n    await TestBed.configureTestingModule({\n      imports: [App],\n    }).compileComponents();\n  });\n\n  it('should create', () => {\n    const fixture = TestBed.createComponent(App);\n    expect(fixture.componentInstance).toBeTruthy();\n  });\n});\n----\n  full. If today is Tuesday: `Today`, `Wednesday`, `Thursday`, `Friday`, `Saturday`.\n- After them, a datepicker for choosing any other date. Dates before today cannot be\n  chosen; there is no upper limit.\n- Exactly one day is selected at a time. When the selected day is one of the five, its\n  button is shown as selected; when it was chosen in the datepicker and is not one of the\n  five, no button is selected and the datepicker shows the date.\n- The selected day is part of the URL: `/?date=<ISO date>`. Choosing a day updates the URL.\n  `/` without `date`, with a date that is not a valid ISO date, or with a date before today\n  selects today.\n\n### 4.2 Movies\n\nMovies and screenings are loaded from the backend each time the screen opens.\n\n- **Loading** — while the requests are in flight the screen shows the text `Loading…` and\n  no movie cards.\n- **Error** — if a request fails, the screen shows the text `Failed to load movies` and a\n  `Retry` button. `Retry` issues the requests again (showing the loading indicator).\n- **Loaded** — a vertical list of movie cards: one per movie that has at least one\n  screening on the selected day, in the order the backend returns the movies. Each card\n  shows:\n  - the title,\n  - the genre,\n  - the runtime as `<runtimeMinutes> min`, e.g. `128 min`,\n  - the format, exactly as in the data: `PL dubbing` or `PL subtitles`,\n  - one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with its time,\n    e.g. `16:00`, ordered by time.\n- **Empty** — when no movie has a screening on the selected day, the screen shows the text\n  `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n\nClicking a screening button opens `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening.\n\n---\n\n----\n# 03: Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel\n\n**What to build:** On the seat map the customer selects and deselects seats and couches, up to 10 seats per booking with a couch counting as 2. Unavailable seats cannot be selected. Exceeding the limit shows a toast. Every state has its colour, the legend explains them, and the selected-seats panel lists the current selection by row.\n\n**Specification:** sections 3.2, 5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 9.2, 9.6, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 02 — Auditorium map.\n\n**Status:** done\n\n- [x] AC-16 — Seats listed in `occupiedSeats` for the screening are rendered unavailable and cannot be selected.\n- [x] AC-17 — A couch is unavailable when either of its two seat identifiers is in `occupiedSeats`.\n- [x] AC-18 — Clicking an available seat selects it; clicking it again deselects it.\n- [x] AC-19 — Clicking a couch selects both of its seats as one unit; it cannot be half-selected.\n- [x] AC-20 — Selection is capped at 10 seats; a couch counts as 2.\n- [x] AC-21 — A click that would exceed 10 seats is ignored and shows the toast `Maximum 10 seats per booking`.\n- [x] AC-22 — At the cap, already selected seats and couches can still be deselected.\n- [x] AC-23 — The legend lists exactly `Available`, `Selected`, `Unavailable`, `Accessible`.\n- [x] AC-24 — Available seats use `#2E7D32`.\n- [x] AC-25 — Selected seats use `#F9A825`.\n- [x] AC-26 — Unavailable seats use `#C62828`.\n- [x] AC-27 — Accessible seats use `#1565C0`.\n- [x] AC-58 — Between the seat map and the `Cancel` / `Continue` buttons, the selected-seats panel shows `Selected seats: <n>` and one `Row <r>: <seats>` line per row, updated on every selection change.\n- [x] AC-66 — Every seat-selection identifier in section 9.2, and the toast identifier in section 9.6, is present with the exact names and values given there.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TuLQ4ngmNdgyyFYRo1pSPq","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"9f8961be-acb9-4b13-a28a-73c78b97ba78","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:56:22.042Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 04"}
