{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AdJ1aQZhPjczuGxogHmnwJ","type":"tool_result","content":"350\t## 6. Summary (`/screenings/:id/summary`)\n351\t\n352\tThe screen loads the screening and its movie. If either cannot be loaded, redirect to `/`.\n353\t\n354\tA title `Your tickets`, then one list item per selected seat and one per selected couch,\n355\tordered by row and then by column. Each item shows:\n356\t\n357\t| Field | Content | Example |\n358\t|---|---|---|\n359\t| movie | the movie title | `The Silent Harbor` |\n360\t| date and time | `<ISO date> <time>` of the screening | `2026-09-15 16:00` |\n361\t| row | the row number | `7` |\n362\t| seat | a seat: its column number; a couch: `Couch <a>-<b>` | `12` / `Couch 3-4` |\n363\t| price | the price from 5.4 | `32.00 PLN` |\n364\t| — | a `Remove` button | |\n365\t\n366\t`Remove` takes the seat or couch out of the booking; the list and the total update at\n367\tonce. Removing the last item opens `/screenings/:id/seats`.\n368\t\n369\tBelow the list: `Total: <sum> PLN`, the sum of the listed prices with two decimals, e.g.\n370\t`Total: 121.00 PLN`.\n371\t\n372\tTwo buttons side by side:\n373\t\n374\t- `Back` returns to `/screenings/:id/seats` with the selection intact.\n375\t- `Confirm` opens `/screenings/:id/checkout`.\n376\t\n377\t---\n378\t\n379\t## 7. Checkout (`/screenings/:id/checkout`)\n380\t\n381\tA title `Your details`, then a form with these fields. The labels of required fields end\n382\twith ` *`.\n383\t\n384\t| Field | Label | Required | Rule | Message when the rule fails |\n385\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n386\t| first name | `First name *` | yes | at least 2 characters | `First name must be at least 2 characters` |\n387\t| last name | `Last name *` | yes | at least 2 characters | `Last name must be at least 2 characters` |\n388\t| email | `Email *` | yes | a valid email address | `Enter a valid email address` |\n389\t| confirm email | `Confirm email *` | yes | identical to Email | `Email addresses do not match` |\n390\t| phone | `Phone number` | no | when filled: exactly 9 digits, nothing else | `Phone number must be exactly 9 digits` |\n391\t| terms | `I accept the terms and conditions *` | yes | checked | `You must accept the terms and conditions` |\n392\t\n393\t- An empty required text field shows `<Label> is required`, with the label without the\n394\t  asterisk, e.g. `First name is required` or `Confirm email is required`. A non-empty field\n395\t  that breaks its rule shows the message from the table. At most one message per field.\n396\t- A valid email address is: one or more characters without spaces or `@`, then `@`, then a\n397\t  domain of characters without spaces or `@` that contains a dot with at least one\n398\t  character on each side, e.g. `anna@example.com`. `not-an-email`, `a@b` and `a@.com` are\n399\t  not valid.\n400\t- Confirm email is compared with Email as typed, whether or not Email itself is valid.\n401\t- Values are validated without trimming, except that an empty phone field is valid.\n402\t- A field's message appears once the field has been left (blurred) at least once, and from\n403\t  then on updates as the value changes. The terms checkbox counts as left once it has been\n404\t  toggled. When the Email value changes, the Confirm email check is re-evaluated.\n405\t\n406\t### 7.1 Keeping the values\n407\t\n408\tThe six values are saved in the booking (section 3.1) as they are typed. Going `Back` to\n409\tthe summary or the seat map and returning, or reloading the page, shows the same values.\n410\tWhether a field was left is not saved: a restored form shows no messages until the\n411\tcustomer leaves a field or clicks `Pay`.\n412\t\n413\t### 7.2 Buttons\n414\t\n415\tTwo buttons side by side: `Back` and the pay button.\n416\t\n417\t- `Back` returns to `/screenings/:id/summary` with the booking intact.\n418\t- The pay button reads `Pay <total> PLN`, e.g. `Pay 121.00 PLN`. It is enabled at all\n419\t  times, except while a payment request is in flight.\n420\t\n421\tClicking the pay button:\n422\t\n423\t- **Invalid form** — marks every field as left, shows every failing message, shows the\n424\t  toast `The form contains errors` and stays on the screen. No request is sent.\n425\t- **Valid form** — sends `POST /reservations` (section 2.2) with the screening id, the\n426\t  booked seat identifiers (in summary order, a couch as its two identifiers), the customer\n427\t  data and the total price. While the request is in flight, the pay button is disabled and\n428\t  reads `Processing…`.\n429\t  - on success: the booking becomes paid, with the customer's email address, and\n430\t    `/confirmation` opens;\n431\t  - on failure: the screen stays as it is, with the values kept, the pay button becomes\n432\t    enabled again and the toast `Payment failed. Please try again.` is shown.\n433\t\n434\t---\n435\t\n436\t## 8. Confirmation (`/confirmation`)\n437\t\n438\t- A heading `Payment successful`.\n439\t- The text `Your tickets will be sent shortly to <email>`, with the email address from the\n440\t  form.\n441\t- A `Continue` button that clears the booking and opens `/`.\n442\t\n443\t---\n444\t\n445\t## 9. Element identifiers\n446\t\n447\tThe QA team's browser automation finds elements by the attributes below. Every element\n448\tlisted must carry exactly this `data-testid` and the listed data attributes. Names and\n449\tvalues are part of the contract: do not rename, abbreviate or prefix them, and do not put\n450\tthese `data-testid` values on any other element.\n451\t\n452\t### 9.1 Movie list\n453\t\n454\t| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n455\t|---|---|---|\n456\t| `day-picker` | container of the day buttons and the datepicker | — |\n457\t| `day-button` | one of the five day buttons | `data-date`, `data-selected` |\n458\t| `date-picker` | the datepicker | — |\n459\t| `movie-list` | container of the movie cards | — |\n460\t| `movies-loading` | loading indicator | — |\n461\t| `movies-error` | element containing the `Failed to load movies` text | — |\n462\t| `movies-retry-button` | `Retry` button | — |\n463\t| `movies-empty` | element containing the `No screenings on this day` text | — |\n464\t| `movie-card` | one movie card | `data-movie-id` |\n465\t| `movie-title` | title inside a card | — |\n466\t| `movie-genre` | genre inside a card | — |\n467\t| `movie-runtime` | runtime inside a card | — |\n468\t| `movie-format` | format inside a card | — |\n469\t| `screening-button` | one screening button inside a card | `data-screening-id` |\n470\t\n471\t### 9.2 Seat selection\n472\t\n473\t| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n474\t|---|---|---|\n475\t| `seat-map-title` | the `Choose your seats` title | — |\n476\t| `seat-map-subtitle` | the `Show Date: …` subtitle | — |\n477\t| `seat-limit-info` | the `You can reserve up to 10 seats per reservation` text | — |\n478\t| `screen-indicator` | the `SCREEN` bar | — |\n479\t| `seat-map` | container of all rows | — |\n480\t| `seat-row` | one row of the auditorium | `data-row` |\n481\t| `row-label-left` | row number at the left edge | `data-row` |\n482\t| `row-label-right` | row number at the right edge | `data-row` |\n483\t| `aisle` | one aisle gap | `data-row` |\n484\t| `seat` | one seat (not a couch) | `data-row`, `data-column`, `data-state` |\n485\t| `couch` | one couch | `data-row`, `data-column-start`, `data-column-end`, `data-state` |\n486\t| `legend` | the legend container | — |\n487\t| `legend-item` | one legend entry | `data-state` |\n488\t| `selected-seats` | the selected-seats panel | — |\n489\t| `selected-seats-count` | the `Selected seats: <n>` line | — |\n490\t| `selected-seats-row` | one `Row <r>: …` line | `data-row` |\n491\t| `cancel-button` | `Cancel` | — |\n492\t| `continue-button` | `Continue` | — |\n493\t\n494\t### 9.3 Summary\n495\t\n496\t| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n497\t|---|---|---|\n498\t| `summary-title` | the `Your tickets` title | — |\n499\t| `summary-list` | container of the summary items | — |\n500\t| `summary-item` | one summary item | — |\n501\t| `summary-item-title` | movie title in an item | — |\n502\t| `summary-item-datetime` | date and time in an item | — |\n503\t| `summary-item-row` | row number in an item | — |\n504\t| `summary-item-seat` | seat description in an item | — |\n505\t| `summary-item-price` | price in an item | — |\n506\t| `summary-item-remove-button` | `Remove` in an item | — |\n507\t| `summary-total` | the `Total: … PLN` line | — |\n508\t| `back-button` | `Back` | — |\n509\t| `confirm-button` | `Confirm` | — |\n510\t\n511\t### 9.4 Checkout\n512\t\n513\t| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n514\t|---|---|---|\n515\t| `checkout-title` | the `Your details` title | — |\n516\t| `first-name-input` | first name field | — |\n517\t| `last-name-input` | last name field | — |\n518\t| `email-input` | email field | — |\n519\t| `confirm-email-input` | confirm email field | — |\n520\t| `phone-input` | phone field | — |\n521\t| `terms-checkbox` | terms checkbox | — |\n522\t| `first-name-label` | first name label | — |\n523\t| `last-name-label` | last name label | — |\n524\t| `email-label` | email label | — |\n525\t| `confirm-email-label` | confirm email label | — |\n526\t| `phone-label` | phone label | — |\n527\t| `terms-label` | terms checkbox label | — |\n528\t| `first-name-error` | first name message | — |\n529\t| `last-name-error` | last name message | — |\n530\t| `email-error` | email message | — |\n531\t| `confirm-email-error` | confirm email message | — |\n532\t| `phone-error` | phone message | — |\n533\t| `terms-error` | terms message | — |\n534\t| `checkout-back-button` | `Back` | — |\n535\t| `pay-button` | the pay button | — |\n536\t\n537\t### 9.5 Confirmation\n538\t\n539\t| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n540\t|---|---|---|\n541\t| `confirmation-heading` | `Payment successful` heading | — |\n542\t| `confirmation-message` | the `Your tickets will be sent shortly to …` text | — |\n543\t| `confirmation-continue-button` | `Continue` | — |\n544\t\n545\t### 9.6 Any screen\n546\t\n547\t| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n548\t|---|---|---|\n549\t| `toast` | the toast, containing its message text | — |\n550\t\n551\t### 9.7 Rules\n552\t\n553\t- `data-state` is exactly one of `available`, `selected`, `unavailable`, `accessible`. A\n554\t  selected accessible seat reports `selected`; an occupied accessible seat reports\n555\t  `unavailable`. Couches never report `accessible`.\n556\t- `data-row`, `data-column`, `data-column-start`, `data-column-end`, `data-movie-id` and\n557\t  `data-screening-id` hold plain numbers, e.g. `data-row=\"7\"`. `data-date` holds an ISO\n558\t  date. `data-selected` is `true` or `false`.\n559\t- `seat`, `couch` and `aisle` elements are inside their `seat-row` element.\n560\t- A `seat` contains only its column number as text; a row label contains only the row\n561\t  number; an `aisle` contains no text.\n562\t- `summary-item-price` contains only the price, e.g. `32.00 PLN`; `summary-item-seat`\n563\t  contains only the seat description, e.g. `12` or `Couch 3-4`; `summary-total` contains\n564\t  only `Total: <sum> PLN`. `selected-seats-count` and each `selected-seats-row` contain only\n565\t  their line.\n566\t- **Library components.** The identifiers of the five text fields, the terms checkbox and\n567\t  the datepicker may be placed either on the native `<input>` itself or on the\n568\t  UI library's component element that contains it. Identifiers of buttons go on the\n569\t  element that receives the click and is disabled when the button is disabled.\n570\t- A field's `-error` element exists in the page only while its message is shown.\n571\t- The `movies-loading` element exists in the page only while loading; `movies-empty` only\n572\t  while the empty text is shown.\n573\t\n574\t---\n575\t\n576\t## 10. Acceptance criteria\n577\t\n578\tEach criterion is either met or not met.\n579\t\n580\t### Movie list\n581\t- **AC-01** — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n582\t- **AC-02** — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n583\t- **AC-03** — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n584\t- **AC-04** — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n585\t- **AC-49** — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n586\t- **AC-50** — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n587\t- **AC-51** — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n588\t- **AC-52** — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n589\t- **AC-53** — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n590\t- **AC-54** — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n591\t- **AC-55** — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.\n592\t\n593\t### Auditorium geometry\n594\t- **AC-05** — The seat map has 15 rows, numbered 1 to 15, row 1 rendered directly under the screen.\n595\t- **AC-06** — Rows 11 to 15 contain 24 columns; rows 1 to 10 contain columns 5 to 24 only.\n596\t- **AC-07** — A two-seat-wide gap is rendered between columns 4 and 5 and between columns 20 and 21 in every row; gaps carry no seat and no number.\n597\t- **AC-08** — Column numbering is global 1–24 and identical across rows; in rows 1–10, numbering starts at 5.\n598\t- **AC-09** — The row number is rendered on both the left and the right edge of every row.\n599\t- **AC-10** — Every seat renders its column number.\n600\t- **AC-11** — A `SCREEN` indicator is rendered above row 1.\n601\t- **AC-12** — Row 1, columns 10 to 15 are accessible seats — 6 of them.\n602\t- **AC-13** — Row 15 renders 12 couches, each spanning two adjacent columns: 1–2, 3–4, … 23–24.\n603\t- **AC-14** — A couch is rendered as one wide element, visually distinct from a single seat.\n604\t- **AC-15** — The total number of selectable elements in the auditorium is 308 (200 seats in rows 1–10, 96 in rows 11–14, 12 couches in row 15).\n605\t- **AC-56** — The seat selection shows the title `Choose your seats` and the subtitle `Show Date: <Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>` of the screening.\n606\t- **AC-57** — Above the seat map, horizontally centred over it, the text `You can reserve up to 10 seats per reservation` is shown.\n607\t\n608\t### Seat selection\n609\t- **AC-16** — Seats listed in `occupiedSeats` for the screening are rendered unavailable and cannot be selected.\n610\t- **AC-17** — A couch is unavailable when either of its two seat identifiers is in `occupiedSeats`.\n611\t- **AC-18** — Clicking an available seat selects it; clicking it again deselects it.\n612\t- **AC-19** — Clicking a couch selects both of its seats as one unit; it cannot be half-selected.\n613\t- **AC-20** — Selection is capped at 10 seats; a couch counts as 2.\n614\t- **AC-21** — A click that would exceed 10 seats is ignored and shows the toast `Maximum 10 seats per booking`.\n615\t- **AC-22** — At the cap, already selected seats and couches can still be deselected.\n616\t- **AC-58** — Between the seat map and the `Cancel` / `Continue` buttons, the selected-seats panel shows `Selected seats: <n>` and one `Row <r>: <seats>` line per row, updated on every selection change.\n617\t- **AC-66** — Every seat-selection identifier in section 9.2, and the toast identifier in section 9.6, is present with the exact names and values given there.\n618\t\n619\t### Legend and colours\n620\t- **AC-23** — The legend lists exactly `Available`, `Selected`, `Unavailable`, `Accessible`.\n621\t- **AC-24** — Available seats use `#2E7D32`.\n622\t- **AC-25** — Selected seats use `#F9A825`.\n623\t- **AC-26** — Unavailable seats use `#C62828`.\n624\t- **AC-27** — Accessible seats use `#1565C0`.\n625\t\n626\t### Pricing\n627\t- **AC-28** — Seats in rows 1–5 cost `25.00 PLN`.\n628\t- **AC-29** — Seats in rows 6–10 cost `32.00 PLN`.\n629\t- **AC-30** — Seats in rows 11–14 cost `39.00 PLN`.\n630\t- **AC-31** — A couch costs `89.00 PLN` per couch, not per seat.\n631\t- **AC-32** — Accessible seats cost `25.00 PLN`, like the rest of row 1.\n632\t\n633\t### Navigation from the seat map\n634\t- **AC-33** — `Cancel` navigates to `/` and clears the selection.\n635\t- **AC-34** — `Continue` navigates to `/screenings/:id/summary`.\n636\t- **AC-35** — `Continue` does nothing when no seat is selected.\n637\t\n638\t### Summary\n639\t- **AC-36** — Each selected item is listed with movie title, screening date, time, row number, seat description and price.\n640\t- **AC-37** — A couch is described as `Couch <a>-<b>`; a single seat is described by its column number.\n641\t- **AC-38** — The total line reads `Total: <sum> PLN` and equals the sum of the listed prices.\n642\t- **AC-39** — `Back` returns to the seat map with the selection intact.\n643\t- **AC-40** — `Confirm` navigates to `/screenings/:id/checkout`.\n644\t- **AC-59** — The summary shows the title `Your tickets`.\n645\t- **AC-60** — Each summary item has a `Remove` button that removes it from the booking and updates the total; removing the last item returns to the seat map.\n646\t- **AC-67** — Every summary identifier in section 9.3 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n647\t\n648\t### Checkout\n649\t- **AC-41** — The form renders first name, last name, email, confirm email, phone number and a terms checkbox.\n650\t- **AC-42** — First name and last name are required and must be at least 2 characters.\n651\t- **AC-43** — Email is required and must be a valid address; confirm email must match it.\n652\t- **AC-44** — Phone number is optional; when filled it must be exactly 9 digits.\n653\t- **AC-45** — The terms checkbox is required.\n654\t- **AC-46** — The pay button is enabled whenever no payment request is in flight; clicking it on an invalid form marks all fields as touched, shows the messages and shows the toast `The form contains errors`, without navigating.\n655\t- **AC-47** — The pay button on a valid form sends `POST /reservations`, is disabled while the request is in flight, navigates to `/confirmation` on success, and on failure stays on the form and shows the toast `Payment failed. Please try again.`\n656\t- **AC-61** — The checkout shows the title `Your details`.\n657\t- **AC-62** — The pay button reads `Pay <total> PLN`, the total of the booking.\n658\t- **AC-63** — `Back` on the checkout returns to the summary with the booking intact.\n659\t- **AC-64** — The checkout values survive going back to the summary and forward again, and a page reload; a new booking starts with an empty form.\n660\t- **AC-65** — The labels of the five required fields end with `*`; the phone label does not.\n661\t- **AC-68** — Every checkout identifier in section 9.4 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n662\t\n663\t### Confirmation and booking\n664\t- **AC-48** — `/confirmation` shows `Payment successful` and `Your tickets will be sent shortly to <email>`; `Continue` navigates to `/` and clears the booking; the booking survives a reload via `sessionStorage`; entering the summary, checkout or confirmation without a matching booking redirects to `/`.\n665\t- **AC-69** — Every confirmation identifier in section 9.5 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n666\t\n667\t---\n668\t\n669\t## 11. Out of scope\n670\t\n671\tDo not build any of these: user accounts, real payment processing, seat locking between\n672\tconcurrent customers, updating `occupiedSeats` after a reservation, posters or images,\n673\tmobile or responsive layouts, keyboard navigation or ARIA beyond what the browser and\n674\tthe UI library give by default, and translations.\n675\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XJiGr3JxWLjX3LmcHjeMGA","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"98c287be-70f3-4d47-a03d-8f9991177af9","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:58:21.432Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 05"}
