{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTYjqFqRWm8a1TVsyah6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015VDhimuvTtPYc36HeJjLHx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app && for f in checkout/checkout.ts checkout/checkout.html checkout/checkout-form.ts checkout/checkout.scss; do echo \"==== $f\"; cat $f; done; echo; cat ../../../../spec/tickets/05-checkout.md | head -60","description":"Print checkout source files and ticket 05"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14056,"cache_read_input_tokens":28155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14056,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NfAHR2fPm1kASehZKanMEu","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"ee6a22e4-35b8-4676-acfd-665fdf1197ca","timestamp":"2026-11-27T13:02:46.805Z","request_id":"req_011ChTYjq4fqvm6HYkJa82ZL","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 06"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015VDhimuvTtPYc36HeJjLHx","type":"tool_result","content":"==== checkout/checkout.ts\nimport { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';\nimport { Component, computed, inject, signal } from '@angular/core';\nimport { takeUntilDestroyed } from '@angular/core/rxjs-interop';\nimport { ReactiveFormsModule } from '@angular/forms';\nimport { MatButtonModule } from '@angular/material/button';\nimport { MatCheckboxModule } from '@angular/material/checkbox';\nimport { MatFormFieldModule } from '@angular/material/form-field';\nimport { MatInputModule } from '@angular/material/input';\nimport { Router } from '@angular/router';\nimport { API_URL } from '../api';\nimport { BookingService } from '../booking';\nimport { NewReservation, Reservation } from '../models';\nimport { ToastService } from '../toast';\nimport { formatPrice, ticketsOf, totalOf } from '../tickets';\nimport { CheckoutField, checkoutErrorMessage, createCheckoutForm } from './checkout-form';\n\nconst FORM_ERRORS_MESSAGE = 'The form contains errors';\nconst PAYMENT_FAILED_MESSAGE = 'Payment failed. Please try again.';\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-checkout',\n  imports: [\n    ReactiveFormsModule,\n    MatButtonModule,\n    MatCheckboxModule,\n    MatFormFieldModule,\n    MatInputModule,\n  ],\n  templateUrl: './checkout.html',\n  styleUrl: './checkout.scss',\n})\nexport class Checkout {\n  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);\n  private readonly router = inject(Router);\n  private readonly toast = inject(ToastService);\n  private readonly booking = inject(BookingService);\n\n  /** The guard only opens this screen for an unpaid booking, so it is present here. */\n  private readonly stored = this.booking.current();\n  private readonly tickets = ticketsOf(this.stored?.seats ?? []);\n  protected readonly total = totalOf(this.tickets);\n\n  protected readonly form = createCheckoutForm(this.stored?.checkout);\n  protected readonly submitting = signal(false);\n  protected readonly payLabel = computed(() =>\n    this.submitting() ? 'Processing…' : `Pay ${formatPrice(this.total)}`,\n  );\n\n  constructor() {\n    // Every change is kept in the booking, so the values survive going back and reloading.\n    this.form.valueChanges.pipe(takeUntilDestroyed()).subscribe(() => this.saveValues());\n  }\n\n  /** The message of a field, or null when it is valid or has not been left yet. */\n  protected error(field: CheckoutField): string | null {\n    return checkoutErrorMessage(this.form, field);\n  }\n\n  protected back(): void {\n    const screeningId = this.booking.current()?.screeningId;\n    if (screeningId !== undefined) {\n      void this.router.navigate(['/screenings', screeningId, 'summary']);\n    }\n  }\n\n  protected pay(): void {\n    if (this.submitting()) {\n      return;\n    }\n    this.form.markAllAsTouched();\n    if (this.form.invalid) {\n      this.toast.show(FORM_ERRORS_MESSAGE);\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const booking = this.booking.current();\n    if (!booking) {\n      void this.router.navigateByUrl('/');\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const values = this.form.getRawValue();\n    const reservation: NewReservation = {\n      screeningId: booking.screeningId,\n      seats: this.tickets.flatMap((ticket) => ticket.seatIds),\n      customer: {\n        firstName: values.firstName,\n        lastName: values.lastName,\n        email: values.email,\n        phone: values.phone,\n      },\n      totalPrice: this.total,\n    };\n\n    this.submitting.set(true);\n    this.http.post<Reservation>(`${API_URL}/reservations`, reservation).subscribe({\n      next: () => {\n        this.booking.save({ ...booking, checkout: values, paidEmail: values.email });\n        void this.router.navigateByUrl('/confirmation');\n      },\n      error: () => {\n        this.submitting.set(false);\n        this.toast.show(PAYMENT_FAILED_MESSAGE);\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  private saveValues(): void {\n    const current = this.booking.current();\n    if (current) {\n      this.booking.save({ ...current, checkout: this.form.getRawValue() });\n    }\n  }\n}\n==== checkout/checkout.html\n<section class=\"checkout-page\">\n  <h1 class=\"title\" data-testid=\"checkout-title\">Your details</h1>\n\n  <form class=\"checkout-form\" novalidate [formGroup]=\"form\" (ngSubmit)=\"pay()\">\n    <mat-form-field class=\"field\">\n      <mat-label data-testid=\"first-name-label\">First name *</mat-label>\n      <input matInput formControlName=\"firstName\" data-testid=\"first-name-input\" />\n      @if (error('firstName'); as message) {\n      <mat-error data-testid=\"first-name-error\">{{ message }}</mat-error>\n      }\n    </mat-form-field>\n\n    <mat-form-field class=\"field\">\n      <mat-label data-testid=\"last-name-label\">Last name *</mat-label>\n      <input matInput formControlName=\"lastName\" data-testid=\"last-name-input\" />\n      @if (error('lastName'); as message) {\n      <mat-error data-testid=\"last-name-error\">{{ message }}</mat-error>\n      }\n    </mat-form-field>\n\n    <mat-form-field class=\"field\">\n      <mat-label data-testid=\"email-label\">Email *</mat-label>\n      <input matInput formControlName=\"email\" data-testid=\"email-input\" />\n      @if (error('email'); as message) {\n      <mat-error data-testid=\"email-error\">{{ message }}</mat-error>\n      }\n    </mat-form-field>\n\n    <mat-form-field class=\"field\">\n      <mat-label data-testid=\"confirm-email-label\">Confirm email *</mat-label>\n      <input matInput formControlName=\"confirmEmail\" data-testid=\"confirm-email-input\" />\n      @if (error('confirmEmail'); as message) {\n      <mat-error data-testid=\"confirm-email-error\">{{ message }}</mat-error>\n      }\n    </mat-form-field>\n\n    <mat-form-field class=\"field\">\n      <mat-label data-testid=\"phone-label\">Phone number</mat-label>\n      <input matInput type=\"tel\" formControlName=\"phone\" data-testid=\"phone-input\" />\n      @if (error('phone'); as message) {\n      <mat-error data-testid=\"phone-error\">{{ message }}</mat-error>\n      }\n    </mat-form-field>\n\n    <div class=\"terms\">\n      <mat-checkbox\n        formControlName=\"terms\"\n        data-testid=\"terms-checkbox\"\n        (change)=\"form.controls.terms.markAsTouched()\"\n        ><span data-testid=\"terms-label\">I accept the terms and conditions *</span></mat-checkbox\n      >\n      @if (error('terms'); as message) {\n      <p class=\"terms-error\" data-testid=\"terms-error\">{{ message }}</p>\n      }\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"actions\">\n      <button mat-stroked-button type=\"button\" data-testid=\"checkout-back-button\" (click)=\"back()\">\n        Back\n      </button>\n      <button mat-flat-button type=\"submit\" data-testid=\"pay-button\" [disabled]=\"submitting()\">\n        {{ payLabel() }}\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  </form>\n</section>\n==== checkout/checkout-form.ts\nimport { FormControl, FormGroup, ValidatorFn, Validators } from '@angular/forms';\nimport { CheckoutValues } from '../booking';\n\nexport type CheckoutField = keyof CheckoutValues;\n\nexport type CheckoutForm = FormGroup<{ [K in CheckoutField]: FormControl<CheckoutValues[K]> }>;\n\n/** One or more characters without spaces or `@`, then `@`, then a domain with a dot that has characters on each side. */\nconst EMAIL_PATTERN = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/;\nconst PHONE_PATTERN = /^\\d{9}$/;\n\n/** Messages by validation error key; the first key of a field that has a message is shown. */\nconst MESSAGES: Record<CheckoutField, Partial<Record<string, string>>> = {\n  firstName: {\n    required: 'First name is required',\n    minlength: 'First name must be at least 2 characters',\n  },\n  lastName: {\n    required: 'Last name is required',\n    minlength: 'Last name must be at least 2 characters',\n  },\n  email: {\n    required: 'Email is required',\n    pattern: 'Enter a valid email address',\n  },\n  confirmEmail: {\n    required: 'Confirm email is required',\n    mismatch: 'Email addresses do not match',\n  },\n  phone: {\n    pattern: 'Phone number must be exactly 9 digits',\n  },\n  terms: {\n    required: 'You must accept the terms and conditions',\n  },\n};\n\nconst EMPTY_VALUES: CheckoutValues = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n  email: '',\n  confirmEmail: '',\n  phone: '',\n  terms: false,\n};\n\n/** Confirm email must equal Email as typed; an empty confirmation is reported by `required` instead. */\nconst matchesEmail: ValidatorFn = (control) => {\n  const email = control.parent?.get('email')?.value;\n  return control.value === '' || control.value === email ? null : { mismatch: true };\n};\n\n/** Builds the checkout form with the given values; without values the form is empty. */\nexport function createCheckoutForm(values: CheckoutValues | undefined): CheckoutForm {\n  const initial = values ?? EMPTY_VALUES;\n  const form: CheckoutForm = new FormGroup({\n    firstName: new FormControl(initial.firstName, {\n      nonNullable: true,\n      validators: [Validators.required, Validators.minLength(2)],\n    }),\n    lastName: new FormControl(initial.lastName, {\n      nonNullable: true,\n      validators: [Validators.required, Validators.minLength(2)],\n    }),\n    email: new FormControl(initial.email, {\n      nonNullable: true,\n      validators: [Validators.required, Validators.pattern(EMAIL_PATTERN)],\n    }),\n    confirmEmail: new FormControl(initial.confirmEmail, {\n      nonNullable: true,\n      validators: [Validators.required, matchesEmail],\n    }),\n    phone: new FormControl(initial.phone, {\n      nonNullable: true,\n      validators: [Validators.pattern(PHONE_PATTERN)],\n    }),\n    terms: new FormControl(initial.terms, {\n      nonNullable: true,\n      validators: [Validators.requiredTrue],\n    }),\n  });\n\n  // The confirmation is compared with Email, so it is checked again whenever Email changes. The\n  // initial check runs now because the control had no parent when it was created.\n  form.controls.email.valueChanges.subscribe(() =>\n    form.controls.confirmEmail.updateValueAndValidity(),\n  );\n  form.controls.confirmEmail.updateValueAndValidity({ emitEvent: false });\n  return form;\n}\n\n/**\n * The message shown for a field: only once the field has been left, and at most one. Null when\n * the field is valid or has not been left yet.\n */\nexport function checkoutErrorMessage(form: CheckoutForm, field: CheckoutField): string | null {\n  const control = form.controls[field];\n  if (!control.touched || !control.errors) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  for (const key of Object.keys(control.errors)) {\n    const message = MESSAGES[field][key];\n    if (message) {\n      return message;\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n==== checkout/checkout.scss\n:host {\n  display: block;\n}\n\n.checkout-page {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 16px;\n  padding: 24px;\n}\n\n.title {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 28px;\n  font-weight: 500;\n}\n\n.checkout-form {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 8px;\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 480px;\n}\n\n.field {\n  width: 100%;\n}\n\n.terms {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 4px;\n}\n\n.terms-error {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: var(--mat-sys-error);\n}\n\n.actions {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 16px;\n  margin-top: 8px;\n}\n\n# 05: Checkout and payment\n\n**What to build:** The customer fills in their details on the checkout form (`Your details`), sees validation messages as they go, can go `Back` to the summary and return — or reload — without losing what they typed, and pays with the `Pay <total> PLN` button. Paying sends the reservation to the backend; success opens `/confirmation`, failure keeps the form and shows a toast.\n\n**Specification:** sections 2.1, 2.2 (`POST /reservations`), 3.1, 7, 9.4, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 04 — Booking and summary.\n\n**Status:** done\n\n- [x] AC-41 — The form renders first name, last name, email, confirm email, phone number and a terms checkbox.\n- [x] AC-42 — First name and last name are required and must be at least 2 characters.\n- [x] AC-43 — Email is required and must be a valid address; confirm email must match it.\n- [x] AC-44 — Phone number is optional; when filled it must be exactly 9 digits.\n- [x] AC-45 — The terms checkbox is required.\n- [x] AC-46 — The pay button is enabled whenever no payment request is in flight; clicking it on an invalid form marks all fields as touched, shows the messages and shows the toast `The form contains errors`, without navigating.\n- [x] AC-47 — The pay button on a valid form sends `POST /reservations`, is disabled while the request is in flight, navigates to `/confirmation` on success, and on failure stays on the form and shows the toast `Payment failed. Please try again.`\n- [x] AC-61 — The checkout shows the title `Your details`.\n- [x] AC-62 — The pay button reads `Pay <total> PLN`, the total of the booking.\n- [x] AC-63 — `Back` on the checkout returns to the summary with the booking intact.\n- [x] AC-64 — The checkout values survive going back to the summary and forward again, and a page reload; a new booking starts with an empty form.\n- [x] AC-65 — The labels of the five required fields end with `*`; the phone label does not.\n- [x] AC-68 — Every checkout identifier in section 9.4 is present with the exact names and values given there.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NfAHR2fPm1kASehZKanMEu","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"889300a0-db49-4f5f-9a55-4ece8b913c16","timestamp":"2026-11-27T13:02:46.820Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 06"}
