{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JFFh1E9dyBBmcko1S9zS4g","type":"tool_result","content":"# 01: Movie list and day picker\n\n**What to build:** A customer opens `/`, picks a day with the day picker (five day buttons and a datepicker), and sees the movies playing that day with their screening times, loaded from the backend, with loading, error and empty states. The selected day lives in the URL. Clicking a screening opens its seat map route. Also sets up the five routes from section 3 (screens 2–5 may be empty placeholders for now) and the redirect of unknown URLs to `/`.\n\n**Specification:** sections 1, 2, 3 (routes), 3.3, 4, 9.1.\n\n**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately).\n\n**Status:** done\n\n- [x] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n- [x] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n- [x] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n- [x] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n- [x] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n- [x] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n- [x] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n- [x] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n- [x] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n- [x] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.\n- [x] AC-51 — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n# 02: Auditorium map\n\n**What to build:** `/screenings/:id/seats` loads the screening and its movie and draws the page header (title, show date, seat-limit text), the `SCREEN` bar and the auditorium: 15 rows with row labels on both edges, both aisles in every row, the entrance gap in rows 1–10, accessible seats in row 1 and 12 couches in row 15. Occupied seats are shown as unavailable. Selection comes in ticket 03. An unknown screening id redirects to `/`.\n\n**Specification:** sections 3.3, 5 (intro and layout), 5.1, 5.3 (colours of available, unavailable and accessible seats), 9.2, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 01 — Movie list and day picker.\n\n**Status:** done\n\n- [x] AC-05 — The seat map has 15 rows, numbered 1 to 15, row 1 rendered directly under the screen.\n- [x] AC-06 — Rows 11 to 15 contain 24 columns; rows 1 to 10 contain columns 5 to 24 only.\n- [x] AC-07 — A two-seat-wide gap is rendered between columns 4 and 5 and between columns 20 and 21 in every row; gaps carry no seat and no number.\n- [x] AC-08 — Column numbering is global 1–24 and identical across rows; in rows 1–10, numbering starts at 5.\n- [x] AC-09 — The row number is rendered on both the left and the right edge of every row.\n- [x] AC-10 — Every seat renders its column number.\n- [x] AC-11 — A `SCREEN` indicator is rendered above row 1.\n- [x] AC-12 — Row 1, columns 10 to 15 are accessible seats — 6 of them.\n- [x] AC-13 — Row 15 renders 12 couches, each spanning two adjacent columns: 1–2, 3–4, … 23–24.\n- [x] AC-14 — A couch is rendered as one wide element, visually distinct from a single seat.\n- [x] AC-15 — The total number of selectable elements in the auditorium is 308 (200 seats in rows 1–10, 96 in rows 11–14, 12 couches in row 15).\n- [x] AC-56 — The seat selection shows the title `Choose your seats` and the subtitle `Show Date: <Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>` of the screening.\n- [x] AC-57 — Above the seat map, horizontally centred over it, the text `You can reserve up to 10 seats per reservation` is shown.\n# 03: Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel\n\n**What to build:** On the seat map the customer selects and deselects seats and couches, up to 10 seats per booking with a couch counting as 2. Unavailable seats cannot be selected. Exceeding the limit shows a toast. Every state has its colour, the legend explains them, and the selected-seats panel lists the current selection by row.\n\n**Specification:** sections 3.2, 5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 9.2, 9.6, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 02 — Auditorium map.\n\n**Status:** done\n\n- [x] AC-16 — Seats listed in `occupiedSeats` for the screening are rendered unavailable and cannot be selected.\n- [x] AC-17 — A couch is unavailable when either of its two seat identifiers is in `occupiedSeats`.\n- [x] AC-18 — Clicking an available seat selects it; clicking it again deselects it.\n- [x] AC-19 — Clicking a couch selects both of its seats as one unit; it cannot be half-selected.\n- [x] AC-20 — Selection is capped at 10 seats; a couch counts as 2.\n- [x] AC-21 — A click that would exceed 10 seats is ignored and shows the toast `Maximum 10 seats per booking`.\n- [x] AC-22 — At the cap, already selected seats and couches can still be deselected.\n- [x] AC-23 — The legend lists exactly `Available`, `Selected`, `Unavailable`, `Accessible`.\n- [x] AC-24 — Available seats use `#2E7D32`.\n- [x] AC-25 — Selected seats use `#F9A825`.\n- [x] AC-26 — Unavailable seats use `#C62828`.\n- [x] AC-27 — Accessible seats use `#1565C0`.\n- [x] AC-58 — Between the seat map and the `Cancel` / `Continue` buttons, the selected-seats panel shows `Selected seats: <n>` and one `Row <r>: <seats>` line per row, updated on every selection change.\n- [x] AC-66 — Every seat-selection identifier in section 9.2, and the toast identifier in section 9.6, is present with the exact names and values given there.\n spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md      | 24 ++++++++++++------------\n spec/tickets/02-auditorium-map.md  | 28 ++++++++++++++--------------\n spec/tickets/03-seat-selection.md  | 30 +++++++++++++++---------------\n spec/tickets/04-booking-summary.md | 36 ++++++++++++++++++------------------\n spec/tickets/05-checkout.md        | 28 ++++++++++++++--------------\n spec/tickets/06-confirmation.md    | 10 +++++-----\n 6 files changed, 78 insertions(+), 78 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md b/spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md\nindex 6a06c27..ac92f2a 100644\n--- a/spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md\n+++ b/spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md\n@@ -6,16 +6,16 @@\n \n **Blocked by:** None (can start immediately).\n \n-**Status:** ready\n+**Status:** done\n \n-- [ ] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n-- [ ] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n-- [ ] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n-- [ ] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n-- [ ] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n-- [ ] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n-- [ ] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n-- [ ] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n-- [ ] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n-- [ ] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.\n-- [ ] AC-51 — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n+- [x] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n+- [x] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n+- [x] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n+- [x] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n+- [x] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n+- [x] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n+- [x] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n+- [x] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n+- [x] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n+- [x] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.\n+- [x] AC-51 — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RXcanrfAdD1yNJ6sy5o99U","session_id":"451a05d2-90d8-4144-a8fc-cedf6ee810e9","uuid":"3151290e-fd23-427f-b31f-9313c93d752e","timestamp":"2026-11-27T13:04:53.885Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 07"}
